==================================================
 EXPERIMENT 1: CORRELATION ANALYSIS
==================================================
Correlation between text length and predicted 'Simple' probability:
 - Pearson r:  0.0839 (p-value: 4.7709e-01)
 - Spearman r: -0.0202 (p-value: 8.6426e-01)
Interpretation:
 - Positive r means longer texts get classified as Simple (LS).
 - Negative r means shorter texts get classified as Simple (LS).
 - Strong correlation (|r| > 0.6) suggests potential length bias.

